La Dolce Vita with Alfa Romeo the most  Italian of car brands the company was  founded in 1910 and has a varied history  this 6c 2500 Super Sport dates back to  the middle of Alfa's hundred year  history it's a car that combines pre-war  motor technology with the aesthetics of  the early post-war era Alfa started  producing the 6c Series in 1927 and the  model was continuously updated until  1953 to keep up with the times  6c stands for Sasa Lindley six cylinders  this 1948 6c already had a two and a  half liter engine and 110 horsepower  right from the word go the engine was  equipped with dual overhead camshafts  but it's special cylinder head is only  part of the Alfa Romeo story the Kawara  sportivo is as popular today with  Italians as it ever was  Mauro kaput see who's a specialist in  Alfa Romeo says he's been driving and  repairing them for more than 30 years he  grew up with them his uncles all drove  Alfa Romeos and he was even driven to  school in one he praises them especially  as a great Drive saying they have a  fantastic sound are very fast and have a  long tradition  this 6c got it's bespoke bodywork from  the touring company in Milan and even  took part in the Mille Miglia  today it's estimated to be worth around  half a million euros  these are Fogler cop says these cars  roughen given these sublime kinds of  body work like this 2500 Supersport with  his short wheelbase only 20 or 23 of  them were ever built  they were the direct forerunner to the  villa desde la cama describes him as one  of alfa romeos crown jewel still today  at least where the six cylinders are  concerned although the bodywork is  constructed from aluminum making it  Superleggera the large alpha feels heavy  and it's steering takes a bit of giving  used to its pre-war vintage workings  mean the driver needs a sensitive touch  when it comes to switching between its  four gears  but not many fans would refuse to take  this car perhaps the most beautiful of  all Alfa Romeos  on the Mille Miglia  perhaps the best words to describe its  Art Deco dashboard a nostalgic flair  would be Cabella machina what a  beautiful car
 

